UI/UX Design Specification
Visual system, page-by-page design, typography, glassmorphism and 3D
1. Design Direction
Clinical-tech rather than sci-fi. The visual system should communicate evidence, calmness and precision. Glassmorphism is a surface treatment, not the information hierarchy. Use 3D primarily for atmosphere and navigation.
2. Color System
Token	Hex	Use
Primary Blue	#0B5FFF	Primary CTA, links, selected filters
Teal	#0E8F8F	Clinical/verified accent
Deep Ink	#122033	Primary text
Slate	#526173	Secondary text
Surface	#F7FAFC	Base background
White	#FFFFFF	Cards
Success	#16845B	Verified/within-budget
Warning	#B7791F	Estimated/stale
Danger	#C53030	Safety/error
Glass Border	rgba(255,255,255,.45)	Glass surfaces
3. Typography
Role	Font	Weight	Size guidance
Display	Inter or Manrope	700–800	44–64px desktop; 34–44px mobile
H1	Inter	700	36–48px
H2	Inter	700	28–36px
Body	Inter	400–500	15–17px
Data	Inter	500–600	14–16px
Labels	Inter	600	12–14px
Chat text	Inter	400–500	15–16px
Avoid decorative display fonts. Medical comparison screens need predictable glyphs, numeric legibility and strong tabular alignment.
4. Glassmorphism Rules
•	Use translucent white surfaces around 60–80% opacity.
•	Backdrop blur 12–24px where supported.
•	Use a 1px low-contrast border.
•	Keep shadows soft and shallow.
•	Never place low-contrast body text directly on busy glass.
•	Critical clinical numbers should sit on opaque/high-contrast surfaces.
5. 3D Background Rules
•	Hero: abstract medical network / orbital nodes / translucent geometry.
•	Search page: subtle animated grid or particles, not a full 3D scene behind data.
•	Hospital detail: optional low-motion depth layer.
•	Comparison: no continuous heavy 3D; use small animated transitions.
•	Mobile: reduce particle count, DPR and animation frequency.
6. Page-by-Page Specification
Page	Layout/content	Visual treatment
Landing/Home	Hero search box; disease/treatment prompt; budget and location quick filters; trust/data provenance strip; example comparisons; chatbot entry.	3D hero background + glass search panel
Search	Left filter rail on desktop; chips on mobile; hospital cards; sort controls; data-confidence badges.	Minimal motion; no distracting 3D
Hospital Detail	Overview, disease treatments, disease-specific outcomes, cost, facilities, accreditation, sources, last updated.	Subtle depth/hover only
Disease Results	Disease title; treatment options; hospitals; disease-specific metrics; cost/location filters.	Animated result transitions
Compare	Side-by-side sticky hospital headers; rows for disease, outcomes, patients treated, cost, distance, facilities, evidence status.	Charts only where data is comparable
Chatbot	Conversation pane + cited hospital cards + comparison drawer + extracted filters.	Animated message entrance, restrained
Source/Evidence	Source document, publisher, reporting period, extracted fields, verification status, conflict history.	No 3D
Admin Verification	Evidence queue; source preview; extracted values; approve/reject/edit; audit history.	Dense professional dashboard
About/Trust	Methodology, ranking explanation, source policy, limitations, privacy.	Static
7. Hospital Card
•	Hospital name + location
•	Relevant speciality
•	Disease/treatment match
•	Disease-specific outcome metric if available
•	Patients treated if available
•	Estimated/published cost range
•	Distance
•	Data confidence
•	Last updated
•	Compare button
8. Comparison UX
Use a horizontally scrollable comparison table on mobile. Pin the hospital name and disease/treatment row. Highlight differences, not winners. Let users expand methodology/source details.
9. Accessibility
•	Keyboard navigation
•	Visible focus states
•	Minimum contrast target of WCAG AA
•	Reduced motion
•	Semantic headings
•	Screen-reader labels for metrics
•	Do not rely on color alone for verification status
